[00:32.97] If my words did glow with the gold of sunshine
[00:41.50] And my tunes were played on the harp unstrung
[00:48.22] Would you hear my voice come through the music?
[00:56.68] Would you hold it near as it were your own?
[01:03.48] It's a hand-me-down, the thoughts are broken
[01:12.06] Perhaps they're better left unsung
[01:19.13] I don't know, don't really care
[01:27.73] Let there be songs to fill the air
[01:37.15] Ripple in still water
[01:43.88] When there is no pebble tossed
[01:48.05] Nor wind to blow
[01:50.99] Reach out your hand, if your cup be empty
[01:59.28] If your cup is full, may it be again
[02:05.84] Let it be known there is a fountain
[02:14.86] That was not made by the hands of men
[02:20.91] There is a road, no simple highway
[02:29.38] Between the dawn and the dark of night
[02:35.99] And if you go, no one may follow
[02:44.82] That path is for your steps alone
[02:54.18] Ripple in still water
[03:00.80] When there is no pebble tossed
[03:04.96] Nor wind to blow
[03:08.35] You who choose to lead must follow
[03:16.35] But if you fall you fall alone
[03:22.98] If you should stand then who's to guide you?
[03:31.67] If I knew the way I would take you home
[03:37.54] 